-- title:
--   Cyclic tame inertia for the Borel action on the j-chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ that is carried to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ by some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$. Let $K\subseteq L((t))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal $(\varpi)$ and $\zeta$ in its image, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of $j_q=t^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral } j\text{-numerator})$. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of the $f$ for which $f\cdot y=x$ for power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal. On the two-chart integral model $X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$), let $z$ be a point at which the germ of $\varpi$, pulled back along $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a maximal point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra $A_1=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ mapping to $z$. Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\varphi:A_1\to\Omega$ a ring homomorphism with kernel $\mathfrak p_y$ such that $\varphi(j)$ is not in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. some elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has a nonzero $q$-torsion point, and assume $W_0$ is centred at $y$: every element of $A_1$ that is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in $\mathfrak p_y$. Finally let $K_0,K_0'\subseteq K$ be the $L$-subfields generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\Gamma_0(M')$- and $\Gamma_0(qM')$-expansion function fields, with $A$ acting compatibly on $K_0'$, let $j_0'\in K_0'$ be nonzero with the same Laurent expansion as $j$, and let $\iota'$ be a ring homomorphism from $A_2=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_0'\,j_0'$ to $A_1$ induced by the inclusion $K_0'\subseteq K$. Then, with $A_1$ an $A_2$-algebra via $\iota'$, there exist a finite group $G$ acting on $A_1$ by ring automorphisms, faithfully and commuting with the $A_2$-action, such that the $G$-invariants of $A_1$ are exactly the image of $A_2$, and a positive integer $e$ such that the inertia subgroup of $\mathfrak p_y$ for this action has cardinality $e$, is cyclic, and $e$ is a unit in $A$.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic input for the study of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ over the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-floor: at a point of the $j$-finite chart lying on the Gauss ($\infty$-Igusa) branch whose $j$-invariant is not supersingular, the covering is Galois with cyclic inertia of order prime to the residue characteristic, that is, tamely ramified. It is used in the proof of regularity of the fibre away from the horizontal sections, the step that feeds Abhyankar's lemma.
